IMPORT prelude

-- Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995 (Singapore) -- the rules a passenger, a member of the public, an operator or an investor meets:
-- operating without a licence (s 12), security screening of train passengers and entrants (s 23A), leaving bicycles and other things
-- on railway premises (s 23B), endangering safety, damage and compensation (ss 25 to 27), evidence of identity (s 39), composition
-- of offences (s 44), and the 5%, 25%, 50% and 75% controller rules for designated entities (ss 21B, 21F, 21G, 21R).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RTSA1995.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 5 of 2026 (in force 4 May 2026) shown. Note that the deposit's arrangement of sections is out of step with the body for
-- Part 6 (it numbers "Power to require evidence of identity" as s 38); the BODY's numbering (s 39) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions with decision content
-- for people outside the Authority. Not encoded: planning and land powers (Part 2, including the owner-initiated acquisition in
-- ss 7 and 7A), the licensing regime's internals (ss 13 to 21: conditions, codes, directions, suspension, winding up), the meaning
-- of equity interest, associate and indirect controller (ss 21C, 21D), the Part 3A remedial directions, inspectors' powers beyond
-- the s 23(3) penalty, special administration (Part 4A), appeals (Part 5), arrest (s 40) and the powers of licensee employees and
-- outsourced enforcement officers (s 41), and the regulations that prescribe which offences may be compounded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995 -- the public`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `12 -- operating without a licence`

-- s 12(1): "Only the Authority or a person licensed by the Authority may operate any rapid transit system." (2): a fine up to
-- $50,000 or 6 months or both "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day during
-- which the offence continues after conviction".
-- s 13(1): the Authority may grant a licence "to any company"; (2) the licensee is authorised for the period in the licence "unless
-- the licence is earlier revoked, cancelled or suspended".
GIVEN `is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may operate a rapid transit system` IF
    `is the Authority` OR `holds a licence in force`

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed operation` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 5000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `23A -- security screening of passengers and entrants`

-- s 23A(1): "It is a condition of entry to any train or railway premises" that a passenger or entrant must, if asked by a police
-- officer or an approved person, undergo screening, a frisk search, or an inspection or search of personal property.
-- (2): a police officer or an APPROVED person may ask the person to (a) walk through a screening detector; (b) pass personal
-- property through an X-ray machine; (c) allow a hand-held scanner to be passed near the personal property; (d) allow the personal
-- property to be inspected; (e) produce or empty the contents of a bag; (f) turn out pockets; (g) remove a coat, jacket, gloves,
-- shoes, hat or other thing worn; (h) open an article for inspection.
-- (3): only a police officer or a SENIOR approved person may ask the person to (a) undergo a frisk search; (b) allow a hand-held
-- scanner to be passed "in close proximity to the train passenger or entrant" (the person, not the property).
-- (9): "approved person" -- an individual authorised by the Authority in writing who is (a) an officer or employee of the Authority;
-- (b) "a member of an auxiliary police force in uniform"; (c) an employee of the licensee; (d) a security officer engaged by the
-- licensee; (e) an outsourced enforcement officer. "senior approved person" -- of those, only (a) auxiliary police in uniform,
-- (b) a licensee's security officer, (c) an outsourced enforcement officer.
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `a police officer in uniform`
    `a police officer not in uniform`
    `an officer of the Authority`
    `an auxiliary police officer in uniform`
    `an auxiliary police officer not in uniform`
    `an employee of the train operator`
    `a security officer engaged by the train operator`
    `an outsourced enforcement officer`

DECLARE Request IS ONE OF
    `walk through a screening detector`
    `pass property through an X-ray machine`
    `allow a scanner over the property`
    `allow the property to be inspected`
    `empty a bag`
    `turn out pockets`
    `remove a coat or shoes`
    `open an article`
    `undergo a frisk search`
    `allow a scanner over the person`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a police officer` IF
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `a police officer in uniform` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer not in uniform` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `authorised in writing by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an approved person` IF
    `authorised in writing by the Authority` AND
        (CONSIDER `the requester`
         WHEN `an officer of the Authority` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an auxiliary police officer in uniform` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an employee of the train operator` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a security officer engaged by the train operator` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `authorised in writing by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a senior approved person` IF
    `authorised in writing by the Authority` AND
        (CONSIDER `the requester`
         WHEN `an auxiliary police officer in uniform` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a security officer engaged by the train operator` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a search of the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`
    WHEN `undergo a frisk search` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `allow a scanner over the person` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `authorised in writing by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requester may ask for it` IF
        `is a police officer` `the requester`
    OR  (IF `is a search of the person` `the request`
         THEN `is a senior approved person` `the requester` `authorised in writing by the Authority`
         ELSE `is an approved person` `the requester` `authorised in writing by the Authority`)

-- s 23A(6): an individual commits an offence if, "without reasonable excuse", he or she refuses or fails to comply with a request or
-- order under (2), (3) or (5); (7) a fine up to $1,000.
-- (8): "However, it is not an offence" to refuse a request made by (a) "a police officer who is not in uniform and who fails to
-- declare his or her office"; or (b) "an approved person who fails to declare his or her office and, in the case of an outsourced
-- enforcement officer, who ALSO refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
-- So a uniformed police officer need declare nothing; an outsourced enforcement officer who has not declared his or her office but
-- produces the card on demand can still be refused only at the passenger's peril.
GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `declared the office` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to produce the identification card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the passenger may refuse without offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `a police officer in uniform` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a police officer not in uniform` THEN NOT `declared the office`
    WHEN `an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN (NOT `declared the office`) AND `refused to produce the identification card`
    OTHERWISE NOT `declared the office`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `authorised in writing by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the request` IS A Request,
      `declared the office` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to produce the identification card` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the request is an offence` IF
        `the requester may ask for it` `the requester` `authorised in writing by the Authority` `the request`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT `the passenger may refuse without offence` `the requester` `declared the office` `refused to produce the identification card`)

-- s 23A(5): where a passenger or entrant refuses (a) to permit screening or inspection of "the personal property" or "any bag,
-- container or other receptacle"; (b) to allow a hand-held scanner near the person or the personal property; or (c) to undergo a
-- frisk search, the officer "may order the train passenger or entrant ... to immediately leave the train or railway premises".
-- "personal property" (9) "does not include clothing being worn". Walking through a screening detector, and removing a coat or
-- shoes, are not in the (5) list. Turning out pockets is treated here as an inspection of personal property (an INFERENCE: (2)(f)
-- speaks of "articles" removed from clothing, which are things carried).
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing it grounds an order to leave` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`
    WHEN `walk through a screening detector` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `remove a coat or shoes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `23B -- leaving bicycles and other things on railway premises`

-- s 23B(1): a person must not cause or allow "any small vehicle, article or thing" to remain on railway premises, or on an adjoining
-- bicycle parking or vehicle set down facility, "so as to create any obstruction or inconvenience to the passage of the public".
-- (2): not if "authorised or permitted by or under this Act or any other Act, or arises out of a lawful and reasonable use".
-- (7): a person must remove it "where directed to do so by an approved person". (11): contravening (1) or (7), or removing or
-- tampering with a removal notice, -- a fine up to $2,000.
GIVEN `it obstructs or inconveniences the public` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised or permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a lawful and reasonable use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaving it there is an offence` IF
    `it obstructs or inconveniences the public` AND (NOT `authorised or permitted by law`) AND (NOT `a lawful and reasonable use`)

-- (4): before moving it, the approved person must take "reasonable steps to inform the owner ... (if known)" and allow or direct
-- the owner to move it. (5): it may be moved IMMEDIATELY where it "is causing obstruction or inconvenience to other persons".
-- That an unknown owner need not be told is an INFERENCE from "(if known)".
GIVEN `causing obstruction to others now` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner is known` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner was told and given a chance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approved person may move it` IF
    `causing obstruction to others now` OR (NOT `the owner is known`) OR `the owner was told and given a chance`

§§ `25 to 27 -- endangering safety, damage and compensation`

-- s 25: any person who "wilfully does or omits to do anything in relation to any railway as a result of which the safety of any
-- person travelling or being upon the railway is endangered, or is likely to be so endangered" -- $10,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 26: any person who "wilfully removes, destroys or damages any railway or railway premises" -- $200,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 27(1): any person who removes, destroys or damages them, "whether wilfully or otherwise", must pay compensation, "in addition to
-- any penalty", recoverable by civil action; (2) the criminal court may assess it and order payment.
GIVEN `acted wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN, `safety endangered or likely to be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence of endangering safety` IF
    `acted wilfully` AND `safety endangered or likely to be`

GIVEN `acted wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN, `damaged the railway or its premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence of damaging the railway` IF
    `acted wilfully` AND `damaged the railway or its premises`

GIVEN `damaged the railway or its premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must pay compensation` IF
    `damaged the railway or its premises`

§§ `39 -- evidence of identity`

-- s 39(1): a police officer or employee of the Authority "who reasonably believes that any person has committed an offence under
-- this Act may require the person to furnish evidence of his or her identity". (2): a person who refuses or "wilfully misstates
-- that information" -- a fine up to $500. No reasonable-excuse defence is written in.
GIVEN `the officer reasonably believes an offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully misstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an identity offence` IF
    `the officer reasonably believes an offence was committed` AND (`refused` OR `wilfully misstated`)

§§ `Penalties and s 44 composition`

-- Maximum fines and terms as written: s 12(2) $50,000 / 6 months; s 21R (all Part 3A offences) $50,000 / 6 months; s 23(3)
-- (failing an inspector's requirement, false information, obstruction) $5,000 / 6 months; s 23A(7) $1,000; s 23B(11) $2,000;
-- s 24(3) (failing the Minister's order to remedy a defect) $5,000 plus $500 a day; s 25 $10,000 / 5 years; s 26 $200,000 /
-- 12 months; s 39(2) $500.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `operating without a licence`
    `a Part 3A controller offence`
    `obstructing an inspector`
    `refusing security screening`
    `obstructing railway premises`
    `failing the Minister's remedy order`
    `endangering safety`
    `damaging the railway`
    `refusing evidence of identity`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `operating without a licence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a Part 3A controller offence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN 5000
    WHEN `refusing security screening` THEN 1000
    WHEN `obstructing railway premises` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing the Minister's remedy order` THEN 5000
    WHEN `endangering safety` THEN 10000
    WHEN `damaging the railway` THEN 200000
    OTHERWISE 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `operating without a licence` THEN 6
    WHEN `a Part 3A controller offence` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN 6
    WHEN `endangering safety` THEN 60
    WHEN `damaging the railway` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 44(1): the Chief Executive or an authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the LOWER of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- prescribed for the offence"; (b) $5,000. Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations (s 44(3)), not retrieved; it is
-- taken here as a fact.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
    ELSE 0

§§ `21B, 21F, 21G, 21R -- controllers of designated entities`

-- s 21B(1): a "5% controller" holds, alone or with associates, "5% or more, but less than 25%" of the equity interests or voting
-- power; a "25% controller" 25% or more but less than 50%; a "50% controller" 50% or more but less than 75%; a "75% controller"
-- 75% or more. The bands do not overlap. (Equity and voting power are alternatives; this encoding takes one percentage, the
-- person's holding or voting power with associates.)
GIVEN `percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the controller band` MEANS
    IF `percent` AT LEAST 75 THEN 75 ELSE IF `percent` AT LEAST 50 THEN 50 ELSE IF `percent` AT LEAST 25 THEN 25 ELSE IF `percent` AT LEAST 5 THEN 5 ELSE 0

-- s 21F(1): "If a person becomes a 5% controller of a designated entity on or after the effective designation date as a result of an
-- INCREASE in the holding of equity interest, or in the voting power controlled", the person "must within 7 days after becoming the
-- 5% controller give written notice to the Authority". (2) An offence; s 21R: $50,000 or 6 months or both, plus $5,000 a day.
-- A fall from 30% to 10% makes the person a 5% controller by a DECREASE, so s 21F does not catch it. A jump from 3% to 30% skips the
-- 5% band, so s 21F does not catch that either (s 21G does).
GIVEN `percent before` IS A NUMBER, `percent after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 5% controller notice is required` IF
        `percent after` GREATER THAN `percent before`
    AND `the controller band` `percent after` EQUALS 5
    AND (NOT (`the controller band` `percent before` EQUALS 5))

-- s 21F(3): a defence if the accused proves "(a) was not aware of the contravention when it occurred; and (b) notified the Authority
-- ... within a period of 14 days after becoming aware". (4): a defence for one who WAS aware if the crossing came from an associate's
-- increase, there is no agreement or arrangement with that associate, and the Authority was notified "within a period of 7 days
-- after the contravention". (5): otherwise lack of intent or knowledge is no defence.
GIVEN `days after becoming a 5% controller when notified` IS A NUMBER, `was aware when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days after becoming aware when notified` IS A NUMBER, `caused by an associate's increase` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has an arrangement with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the contravention when notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 5% controller is guilty` IF
        `days after becoming a 5% controller when notified` GREATER THAN 7
    AND (NOT ((NOT `was aware when it occurred`) AND `days after becoming aware when notified` AT MOST 14))
    AND (NOT (`was aware when it occurred` AND `caused by an associate's increase` AND (NOT `has an arrangement with that associate`)
              AND `days after the contravention when notified` AT MOST 7))

-- s 21G(1): "Except with the prior written approval of the Authority, a person must not" (a) by an increase, "become a 25% controller,
-- 50% controller or 75% controller", or (b) by a decrease, "cease to be a 25% controller, 50% controller or 75% controller", of a
-- designated entity on or after the effective designation date. (2): not where the transaction "is entered into before the
-- effective designation date". A move WITHIN one band (30% to 45%, 80% to 100%) changes nothing; a SALE down from 30% to 10% needs
-- approval just as a purchase up to 30% does.
GIVEN `percent before` IS A NUMBER, `percent after` IS A NUMBER, `transaction entered before designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prior approval of the Authority is required` IF
        (NOT `transaction entered before designation`)
    AND (NOT (`the controller band` `percent before` EQUALS `the controller band` `percent after`))
    AND ((`the controller band` `percent before` AT LEAST 25) OR (`the controller band` `percent after` AT LEAST 25))

-- s 21R: every Part 3A offence -- a fine up to $50,000 or 6 months or both, and a further $5,000 "for every day or part of a day"
-- the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `days or part days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a Part 3A offence` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 5000 TIMES `days or part days continued after conviction`
